Voice Button includes third-party components.

Voice Button source code: https://github.com/machine202502/voice-button
Voice Button source license: MIT, see LICENSE.
Copyright (c) 2026 machine202502.

The executables contain Rust crates and native libraries:
  - ONNX Runtime (MIT) - runs the sherpa-onnx model sessions;
  - sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0) - the speech engine: NeMo/GigaAM and the
    multilingual ONNX models, including their feature extraction;
  - whisper.cpp (MIT) - the Whisper speech engine;
  - Vulkan Loader (Apache-2.0, Khronos Group) - lets the app start and use
    Vulkan for whisper.cpp; the vendor driver supplies the actual ICD.
Their names, versions, authors, repositories, and available license texts are
collected in THIRD-PARTY.txt next to the executables in release packages, and
the license texts themselves are in the licenses/ directory of this repository.

The Windows packages also carry the Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable
(vc_redist.x64.exe and its runtime DLLs), redistributed under the Microsoft
Visual Studio license terms, and install it silently when setup runs.

Bundled sound cues start.wav and end.wav are dedicated to the public domain
under CC0 1.0. Their sources and processing are documented in assets/CREDITS.md.

Speech models are not bundled with Voice Button. The application only offers
links from which the user can download them. No model license or model source
notice is required for those recommendations in this package.
